{"name":"Almost Apricot","hex":"#e0a787","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"almost","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Very close to, but not quite.","Up to, except for a negligible set (where negligible is not universally but contextually defined)."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Something or someone that doesn't quite make it."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/almost"},{"term":"apricot","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A round sweet and juicy stone fruit, resembling peach or plum in taste, with a yellow-orange flesh, lightly fuzzy skin and a large seed inside.","The apricot tree, Prunus armeniaca."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a pale yellowish-orange colour, like that of an apricot."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/apricot"}],"entries":[{"title":"Almost","blocks":[{"text":"In set theory, when dealing with sets of infinite size, the term almost or nearly is used to refer to all but a negligible amount of elements in the set. The notion of \"negligible\" depends on the context, and may mean \"of measure zero\", \"finite\", or \"countable\"."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Almost","wikidata":"Q840148"},{"title":"Apricot","blocks":[{"text":"An apricot is a fruit, or the tree that bears the fruit, of several species in the genus Prunus. Usually an apricot is from the species Prunus armeniaca, but the fruits of the other species in Prunus sect. Armeniaca are also called apricots. In 2023, world production of apricots was 3.7 million tonnes, led by Turkey with 20% of the total."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Apricot_and_cross_section.jpg/330px-Apricot_and_cross_section.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apricot","wikidata":"Q3733836"},{"title":"Apricot (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Apricot is a light yellowish-orangish color that is similar to the color of a